{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Provision the local accounts designer, reviewer, and visitor.","status":"satisfied","summary":"All three accounts were created and directly observed both before and after the node restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-39007c6679f44ddb","cmd-907e6eaef1c84543","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"New subdirectories and documents created by designer inherit reviewer read/write access while remaining owned by designer.","status":"satisfied","summary":"A designer-created subdirectory and file under umask 077 remained designer-owned, inherited the configured ACLs, and were successfully read and modified by reviewer. The behavior was repeated successfully after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8fe8f94a6599479e","cmd-907e6eaef1c84543","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Visitor has no access to the project directory or designer-created documents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Direct visitor directory-listing and document-read attempts were denied before restart, and both denials were reproduced after restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8fe8f94a6599479e","cmd-907e6eaef1c84543","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Provide persistent inheritance without a periodic permission-repair job.","status":"satisfied","summary":"Default ACLs were installed on the project directory and automatically propagated to newly created nested content. The complete command trace contains no creation of a cron job, timer, or other periodic repair mechanism, and inheritance continued after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-39007c6679f44ddb","cmd-8fe8f94a6599479e","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6"]},{"id":"R5","requirement":"Preserve the existing project contents.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The original brief.txt retained its baseline SHA-256 hash throughout, temporary project test directories were removed, and the final project listing contained only the original file.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-39007c6679f44ddb","cmd-907e6eaef1c84543","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6"]},{"id":"R6","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use compatible software.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were unchanged from the lifecycle baseline through the post-executor snapshot. ACL support was installed from the native CentOS repository, and package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8cc350b9e09d4e20","cmd-60b371284a524e03","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.95,"summary":"All substantive mutations had clear task or verification roles: installing ACL utilities, provisioning accounts, configuring ACLs, creating bounded access tests, cleaning those project tests, and performing the mandatory restart. The only unnecessary retained mutation/residue was four small /tmp capture files created during visitor-denial testing—visitor-ls.out, visitor-ls.err, visitor-cat.out, and visitor-cat.err—which remained after execution rather than being removed. No failed services, new listeners, or package-health damage were observed. The reboot-related systemd-private directory changes and PID changes are normal restart effects.","evidence_ids":["cmd-60b371284a524e03","cmd-39007c6679f44ddb","cmd-8fe8f94a6599479e","cmd-907e6eaef1c84543","cmd-696daf763d3e4ac4","cmd-eeb57748a9b94ff6","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"All material task outcomes are satisfied with direct behavioral evidence. The provider-wide restart protocol is also complete: node1 had a healthy pre-restart state and boot ID, an acknowledged restart, a different post-restart boot ID corroborated by lifecycle snapshots, and recovered accounts, ACLs, preserved data, and access behavior.","limitations":["There was no dedicated inventory of cron jobs or timers, although the complete executor timeline shows no periodic repair mechanism being created and the observed default-ACL behavior directly demonstrates inheritance.","Four visitor-test capture files were left in /tmp; this affects hygiene but not task functionality."]}
